WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.230
<i>It's the semifinals against Yoin High,</i>

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.900
<i>led by the Emperor, Tooru Asuka.</i>

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.820
<i>After taking the field early in the game,</i>

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.190
<i>Kakeru boldly used his Phi Trick</i>

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.930
<i>when facing Asuka-san for the first time,</i>

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.740
<i>then fought to assist Araki-san's shot,</i>

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.120
<i>giving Enoshima the first goal.</i>

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.040
<i>However, Yoin came back and 
used an unexpected strategy,</i>

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.040
<i>in which Asuka-san was bait, 
and tied up the game,</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.580
<i>showing their deep inner strength.</i>

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>Yoin is strong, but the 
match is just beginning.</i>

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:06.060
<b>Desperate Situation</b>

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:10.440
<b>Enoshima            Yoin</b>

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.360
The score is 1-1, still a tie,

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.070
with only moments left in the half.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.480
The two aces, Araki and 
Asuka, are facing off.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.450
Amazing.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.330
Yoin is completely shutting down 
all the Enoshima attackers.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.050
Even if they manage to get the ball,

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:29.420
they won't be able to move
 forward, or even pass it on.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.130
Won't it be up to Kakeru then, Sera?

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.090
Kakeru should be able to 
slip past his defender

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.420
and get open.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.170
That won't happen.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.630
Look at Asuka's positioning.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.850
While sparring with Araki,

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:47.270
he's blocking off his 
through pass options.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.480
They're still going. 
It's a long face-off.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.940
Araki still has the ball, 
but he's got nowhere to go.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.820
<i>Damn it. There aren't any gaps.</i>

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.780
Araki!

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.070
Oda is running up behind Araki!

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.530
Here goes nothing.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.330
Oda's middle shot.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.750
But Asuka slides in!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.840
The ball rolls into the vital area.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.470
The first one to get there is...

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.300
I can make it.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.470
Aizawa!

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.930
Out of nowhere, Aizawa comes 
running for the free ball.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.760
Is this the intuition of a striker?

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:27.810
Keeper!

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.020
Okay!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.400
The course...

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.400
Aizawa shoots!

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:41.450
Close! The ball is just 
outside the goal.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.910
Enoshima didn't get that goal.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.870
Mishima-san, how much 
time in the first half?

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.460
Oh, sure.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.960
There's three minutes, plus loss time.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.830
If we're going to play our 
hand, it has to be now.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.380
That was close, Aizawa.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.470
I'm sorry. 
I know I had to make it.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.510
It's Asuka.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.050
Huh?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.560
At the same time he calls 
out to the keeper,

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.510
he's organizing the defenders,

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:10.100
telling them where your shot will go.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.480
He's a real pain.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.940
Enoshima is making a substitution.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.150
It's finally my time!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:18.820
It's Nakatsuka.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:23.110
Coming in for Yakumo is the 
first year, Kota Nakatsuka.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.370
Good work. Leave the rest to me.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.080
Don't take them lightly.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.790
All right! I'm gonna push 'em back!

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.380
Sawamura moves from the 
left side to the right,

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.750
and Nakatsuka comes in for 
the left defensive middle.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.630
Coach, even though we've increased

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.050
the number of offensive players,

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.010
matching up Nakatsuka 
with Onimaru-san seems...

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.430
Wouldn't it be better to keep 
Sawamura-san on the left side?

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.560
It's true that Sawamura-kun's tough defense

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.520
was difficult for Onimaru-kun,

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.060
but that last goal occurred

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.400
because Yoin changed their strategy.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.480
When Onimaru-kun cuts towards the goal,

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.950
Sawamura will be his opponent,

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:06.860
but to prevent a fast dribble 
down the sidelines,

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.760
we need Kota-kun's speed.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.960
Honestly, it's a gamble,

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.580
but if we don't do something,

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.420
we can't prevent them from scoring.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.630
Still,

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:20.550
I'm worried about Nakatsuka's defense.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.380
It's all right.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.720
I've told Kota-kun what he needs to do.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.060
I'll have him running non-stop

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.140
between offense and defense

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.350
and get rid of this bad mood 
with his energetic attitude.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.690
All right! All right!

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.770
If you get the ball, 
pass it to the sides!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.310
You stay back!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.730
Sides! Sides!

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.360
The game restarts with Yoin's goal kick.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.780
The short ball goes to Sendo.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.530
Sendo sends the ball to 
Shiratori on the side.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.820
I'll stop you here.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.250
The forward, Hino, moves 
in for a fast check.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.330
The ball goes from Shiratori 
to Asuka in the middle.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:55.200
Onimaru!

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.210
To Onimaru. His opponent is...

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.170
Nakatsuka! This is their first match up.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.970
Be careful, Nakatsuka!

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.630
Kota-kun! Go for it!

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.300
Leave it to me!

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:09.970
I knew it.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.930
Onimaru is running up the side... Wait!

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.890
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.890
It's Nakatsuka.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:18.150
Onimaru slipped past Nakatsuka once,

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.280
but out of nowhere, Nakatsuka 
is again on Onimaru's back.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.530
<i>This guy...</i>

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:24.820
This is where it starts.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:30.160
Kota-kun will be able to keep 
up with Onimaru's speed.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.450
After all, he may look 
like that, but he can run

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.990
50 meters in 6.2 seconds.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.670
He's faster than me?

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.300
Really? I didn't know that.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.210
He isn't very good at dribbling,

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:42.670
so it may not look like it,

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.300
but if he's just running,

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.710
Onimaru-kun won't easily shake him off.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.090
In order to lower the risk

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.810
of an open sideline shot 
from in front of the goal,

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:55.390
I wanted to put him in, 
even if it's just for speed.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.770
Nakatsuka's fast!
 He's closing in on Onimaru.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:58.520
Kota!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.810
Not bad.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.530
This time I've put Kota-kun in,

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.860
not for attack,
 but to defend the sidelines.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.860
Nakatsuka's caught Onimaru!

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.070
I'm not letting you get away!

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.580
Onimaru leave Nakatsuka 
and cuts into the middle.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.000
This could be dangerous.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.200
You're not getting through.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.340
But here's Oda.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.590
In a simple one-on-one, 
this man is hard to shake.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.670
This is good.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.260
Now there won't be a repeat of 
the play that let them score.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.600
Yoin makes a big side change.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.600
The ball flies with perfect accuracy 
to Shiratori on the opposite side.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.560
All right.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.520
I won't let you. I'll stop you.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.110
He had trouble against Onimaru,

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.900
but Sawamura isn't falling 
for Shiratori's feints.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.070
Shiratori!

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.440
Here's Asuka.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.620
The dangerous man 
who uses the whole field

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:53.280
appeared on the left side,

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.620
as if he knew this side 
change was going to occur.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.080
I won't let you.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.290
Aizawa was chasing down Asuka.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.790
Did these two know where 
the ball would be?

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.590
<i>I'll stop him here and 
give it to Araki-san.</i>

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.090
Hino is moving in to join them.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.550
What will you do, Emperor Tooru Asuka?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.510
A-A long shot?

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.970
Asuka goes for a long 
shot with his left foot.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:23.650
<i>No. If he was shooting from the left side</i>

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:25.900
<i>he would use his right 
foot to apply a hook.</i>

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:26.900
<i>This is...</i>

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.360
No! This is a long pass to 
Onimaru on the opposite side.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:35.860
Onimaru has outrun Nakatsuka 
in a free sprint.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:38.410
<i>We did this hundreds of times in practice.</i>

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.710
<i>Because we practiced and practiced,</i>

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.330
<i>I can confidently run towards this point.</i>

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.420
<i>Believing that Asuka-san's 
pass will land here.</i>

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.840
The pass, cutting a diagonal 50 meters 
across the Enoshima defense,

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.300
is going to Onimaru.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.300
<i>I don't believe it.</i>

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:56.760
<i>What a guy.</i>

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.720
<i>Watch carefully, Enoshima.</i>

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.140
<i>No matter how difficult the opponent,</i>

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:07.100
<i>to protect the legacy of our 
senpais who won in the end...</i>

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.030
<i>We can't lose!</i>

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:17.370
<i>The burdens we carry are different!</i>

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:25.960
<i>This is...</i>

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.090
<i>Yoin's soccer.</i>

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.130
Goal!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:37.140
At the end of the first half,
 Yoin's Ikusa scores.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:41.390
It's 1-2, Enoshima allowed 
them a comeback goal.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.020
Damn it.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.930
Snap out of it! 
We'll take it right back.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.650
Don't worry. 
We're restarting right away.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.240
That was the referee's whistle.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:55.610
Enoshima gives away the comeback 
goal and the first half ends.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.070
I was naive.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:02.040
Even though Nakatsuka

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.870
was able to stop Onimaru-san's 
fast dribble once...

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.960
Yes. However,

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.840
Onimaru-kun escaped his mark 
by making a side change

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:12.300
and ran for that spot,
 just before the end line,

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:15.300
where Asuka-kun sent his long pass.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.050
I can't believe they planned 
this kind of formation play

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.760
in the event that there would be

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.680
a defender who could keep 
up with Onimaru-kun.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.810
After allowing a goal at 
the end of the first half,

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.770
when you should never lose a point,

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.690
how will Enoshima recover 
in the second half?

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.280
I don't know about recovering.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.450
That goal wasn't because 
Enoshima's defense fell apart.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.530
Kakeru seemed to be doing well, too,

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:42.240
so who knows what will happen.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.580
They're playing against 
Yoin's Asuka-san.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:51.170
Your friends knew best that 
that goal was critical.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.170
Kakeru is the striker that 
Suguru was searching for.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.090
He isn't the kind of guy who would 
give up over something like this.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:57.890
Suguru?

00:10:58.470 --> 00:10:59.760
You mean, Suguru Aizawa?

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.640
Yeah. Kakeru is Suguru's 
younger brother.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.720
If what happened hadn't occurred,

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:10.610
Suguru would be playing in Kama's 
below top: your position.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:15.320
<i>That's right. Kakeru won't give up now.</i>

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.240
You're going no matter what, Kakeru?

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.620
Yep. I just have to see what 
it's like to play with

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.280
this Araki-san who my 
brother acknowledged.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.790
So then you'll never 
receive my passes again.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.200
That's not true.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.420
In the junior league or for the country,

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.210
our soccer will continue.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:35.920
Kakeru...

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.010
I decided that I'll 
never run away again.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.130
Yusuke!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.350
Yusuke!

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.930
What's wrong, Yusuke? 
You were spacing out.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.060
Sorry, Kunimatsu-san.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.810
How's Kakeru— I mean, how's Enoshima?

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.310
Yeah.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:57.480
Everyone, you understand 
the coach's instructions?

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:01.070
Even when the ball goes 
to the opposite side,

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.700
Nakatsuka will stay on Onimaru.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.870
Wait for the signal to 
go on the offensive.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.040
Got it!

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:09.120
Defenders, don't neglect 
following up on the sidelines,

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.410
and be careful of Asuka's overlap.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.210
Okay!

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.580
Crush, crush, crush!

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:18.050
We've got to score a goal.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:21.630
Yes. I'll definitely do 
my job as a striker.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:23.550
You said it.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:26.140
Then let's win and eat some yakiniku.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.890
Let's win this match!

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.060
Yeah!

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.500
Five minutes into the second half.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.950
The score is 1-2, Yoin's lead.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.180
It's Enoshima's ball at midfield.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.910
What will you do, Araki?

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:55.550
Is this a plan to protect 
their one goal lead?

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.380
The withdrawn Yoin shows no 
signs of active movement.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:01.730
<i>Now then...</i>

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:04.310
<i>As long as Asuka-kun is 
in front of the goal,</i>

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.800
<i>we cannot easily get behind 
the defensive line.</i>

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:11.770
<i>Falling for their offsides 
trap is just what Yoin wants.</i>

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:16.700
<i>They aren't an opponent that 
we can easily dribble past.</i>

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:19.950
<i>Their defense isn't just 
good at one-on-one,</i>

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:21.730
<i>they're good at using 
everyone around them.</i>

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:26.200
Looking for Araki's pass, Aizawa 
is heading into the vital area.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:29.420
Kakeru.

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:31.550
Yes.

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.090
Do you remember?

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:33.620
Huh?

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:39.080
We'll break through their iron 
defense with a pass of our own.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:43.600
Yes!

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:46.730
What's wrong? 
Aren't you attacking?

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.820
Araki, still at midfield, isn't moving.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.020
Is he carefully deciding his play?

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:54.820
Will he go to one of his wings

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.770
or towards the back of 
the defense using Aizawa?

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.490
<i>Let's go with that.</i>

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:03.330
It's to Takase.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:06.240
But did he miskick? 
The pass is long.

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:08.460
All right. Side out.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:12.660
Takase jumps!

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.240
What?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.470
He's good.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:17.460
He drops the high ball with 
a header behind Yoin's Maya

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.260
and breaks into a sprint.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:25.310
A wing player with that height is rare,

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:29.090
so the defense isn't used to 
that sort of sideline high ball.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:33.070
Using that, we can get past 
the defense during their

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:35.280
momentary delay and 
cut diagonally across.

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.780
Takase is within middle shot distance,

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:40.700
but Araki is heading into 
the vital area as well.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.910
<i>I'll give this to Araki-san.</i>

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.620
He sends it to Araki.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.860
Hino is coming in from the right side

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.500
and Takase, who just passed,

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:51.820
is heading into the area as well.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.130
Ohtsuki, cover number 9.

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:56.120
Mukai, a little forward.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.040
<i>Aizawa is still in the vital area.</i>

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.460
Araki passes to Aizawa behind him

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.050
and he runs into the area!

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:08.810
What?

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:11.400
But then Kakeru-kun's 
pass will be offsides.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:13.470
No. They're aiming for...

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:17.890
A middle shot!

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:18.910
What?

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:21.900
The goal keeper is distracted 
by Araki and isn't prepared.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.860
The tying score is heading for the goal!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.030
Asuka hits it,

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.990
but the ball is still 
heading for the goal!

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:39.970
An exciting middle shot 
against the defense

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:41.640
which was looking for an offsides.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:43.970
It was so close, it hit the bar.

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.210
Damn it.

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:48.440
So close.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:50.170
No, that was fine.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:54.150
Now that we've show them 
Kakeru-kun's powerful middle shot,

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:57.640
if Araki-kun or Mako-kun 
can shoot aggressively...

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:00.350
Those two really did it.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.520
Fearing a middle shot,

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.020
the defense will move up and

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.320
create a chance to take their back.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.830
It's what was used in the 
inter-high game against

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.360
the withdrawn and hardened SC defense.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.780
Nice, Asuka.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:16.380
What's wrong?

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:19.800
It appears that it's still 
early for the total defense.

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:20.470
Huh?

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:22.540
We're going to get another goal,

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.960
to take away the chance 
of an unexpected play.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:28.430
It's Araki's corner kick.

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.390
They've still got a chance.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.130
It's up!

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.300
The ball is deflected 
in a rough contest.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:39.530
It's Aizawa!

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:41.730
But Asuka marks him.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.740
Aizawa takes a hard shot.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:46.290
How rare.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:49.870
Asuka doesn't take 
single marks like that.

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.670
It's because he's Suguru's brother.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:55.660
Back when Asuka and I were 
juniors at Yokohama,

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:59.210
we had a match against Kama.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:00.880
Remember, Kunimatsu?

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:03.890
Yes. I was on the bench,

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:05.850
but Suguru was already wearing number 10

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:08.380
for Kama by the summer of his first year.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:11.350
It was a practice match,

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.020
but Suguru had just returned from

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:14.840
his representation tour in Europe.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:19.350
<b><i>Yokohama</i></b>

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:19.350
<b><i>Kama High</i></b>

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:19.350
Suguru appeared 15 minutes 
before the end of the match.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.860
He was probably jetlagged 
and it was a practice match,

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.370
so the coach probably didn't 
intend to put him in.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:27.150
But...

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:32.410
at the moment,
 even though it was 2-0

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:34.820
and I don't know why, 
he said he wanted to go in.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:38.380
He said he ran there, 
so he didn't need a warm up,

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:40.300
and he begged the coach.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:43.200
With 10 minutes left, 
he went onto the field.

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:45.840
I was a little excited.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:48.290
I was going to see the true 
strength of a genius player.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:51.980
After all, after Suguru went 
to Kama High school,

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.480
he had a number of representative 
matches and tours so,

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.310
practices against teammates aside,

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:58.820
I never had the chance to see him play

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.070
against a strong opponent,

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:01.680
even though I had been on his team.

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:05.280
I still remember those 
10 minutes clearly.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.900
The game changed after Suguru went in...

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.870
In the end, he scored 2 goals

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.330
and 1 assist in those 10 minutes

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.170
and turned the game on its head.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:24.470
Well, at that time, neither I nor Asuka

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:27.120
was at a representative level.

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:31.100
Wearing the Japanese flag,
 touring the world,

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:36.090
coming back twice as good, 
Suguru easily kicked us aside.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:38.230
That's an amazing story.

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:41.940
Since then, I've practiced furiously.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:44.530
I chose Kama as my high 
school without hesitation

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:46.530
and turned down the youth invitations

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:48.450
and decided to play club...

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:50.060
Because of Suguru-san.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.460
It's an old story,

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:58.580
but Asuka probably 
experienced something similar.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:03.630
<i>Takajo-san, you're always 
looking critically at Kakeru,</i>

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:07.970
<i>but it also means 
he's got your attention,</i>

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.930
<i>because he's Suguru-san's little brother.</i>

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:12.100
<i>No, maybe he has something</i>

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:13.890
<i>that Suguru-san didn't have.</i>

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:17.970
<i>Maybe Takajo-san and 
Asuka-san see that in him...</i>

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.400
Aizawa, middle shot!

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.810
This time the keeper catches it.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:32.600
Kakeru!

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:45.660
I wonder if Kake-nii is okay.

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.300
He looks like he's in pain.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:52.680
Aizawa is after the ball.
 Will he reach it?

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:57.430
It's almost time to go home, you two.

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:58.590
Just a little longer!

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:05.470
Goal!

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:08.140
You're a cheater, Brother!

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.860
That makes it 9-0.

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:13.330
If I score one more goal, it's over.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:16.080
I won't lose. It's my turn next.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:16.940
Honestly...

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.860
Suguru, you really like soccer.

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:21.790
Yep. I love it!

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:25.840
I going to win the World 
Cup, when I grow up.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:27.580
Oh, shoot.

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:32.120
Kakeru...

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:37.850
Amazing, Kakeru. 
That was an amazing shot.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:41.840
Brother, can I go to the World Cup, too?

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:44.800
Let's go together, Kakeru. 
It's a promise.

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:52.950
Your father will be home soon. Let's go.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:58.200
Soccer is fine, but don't 
do anything dangerous.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.580
Don't worry.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:02.000
I'll protect Kakeru.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.250
Forever and ever.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:04.790
Yeah!

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:09.700
Aizawa faces the defense again!

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:14.260
Go, Enoshima!

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:15.870
Go, Kake-nii!

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:19.930
Go, Kakeru.

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:27.360
Araki!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.860
Hyodo's middle shot!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.450
Damn. No good.

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:37.060
We'll shoot as many times as it takes.

00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:41.080
Kakeru's being completely marked.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:44.920
He can get free in the vital area,

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:48.750
but in the penalty area, 
Asuka-san is marking him.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:51.040
It's probably pretty hard on him.

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:54.000
<i>Asuka-san is probably thinking,</i>

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:58.210
<i>if something is going to happen,
 Kakeru holds the key.</i>

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:02.630
Oda overlaps and shoots!

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:05.230
Inaba clears it.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:08.110
Enoshima continues to 
shoot middle shots.

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:09.820
I see.

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:11.940
By repeatedly taking middle shots,

00:22:11.940 --> 00:22:14.240
the defensive line moves up.

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:17.560
They're making space 
behind for Kakeruchhi.

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:19.450
If all goes well.

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:22.750
But if Asuka reads him, 
they could be in trouble.

00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:27.840
<i>Still, if they don't go that 
far, it isn't any fun.</i>

00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:31.170
<i>Keep pushing harder, harder, harder.</i>

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:34.930
Oda slowly dribbles into the defense.

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:37.550
On either side are Hyodo and Araki,

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:39.180
but will they keep 
shooting from the middle?

00:22:41.600 --> 00:22:42.590
Watch number 8!

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:44.480
He's got a middle shot as well.

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:45.550
Cut to the right!

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:49.480
There are two defenders on him.

00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:51.610
Will Araki be able to hold on to the ball?

00:22:51.610 --> 00:22:54.280
<i>I'll show you the best drama.</i>

00:22:55.490 --> 00:22:56.890
It's a one-touch pass.

00:22:57.570 --> 00:22:59.350
<i>I've set the stage.</i>

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:00.770
It's to Hino?

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:03.230
<i>Follow me. This ball is...</i>

00:23:03.790 --> 00:23:04.690
Takase?

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:07.150
<i>This ball is definitely through.</i>

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:09.150
No, it's through...

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:12.240
The one who's waiting for the ball is...

00:23:12.340 --> 00:23:13.880
Aizawa!

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:15.200
<i>It connected!</i>

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:18.160
<i>Do what a striker is supposed to do!</i>

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:21.560
<i>The entire offense's 
spirit is together and</i>

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>they've made it behind the 
back line into critical space.</i>

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:29.560
Kakeru, make it.

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:30.480
Aizawa!

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:31.070
Go!

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:32.050
We're counting on you!

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:33.100
Kakeru!

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:36.700
Wearing number 11, 
Kakeru Aizawa is running in.

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:38.700
Put the tying point in the goal, Kakeru!

00:23:38.700 --> 00:23:41.410
<i>This is the chance that everyone 
worked together to make.</i>

00:23:41.410 --> 00:23:43.060
<i>I definitely won't waste it.</i>

00:23:43.580 --> 00:23:45.000
<i>The keeper is right handed,</i>

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:46.530
<i>he won't reach the opposite corner.</i>

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:48.030
<i>Don't float it over.</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:49.990
<i>Push it straight in.</i>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:51.450
<i>Go!</i>

00:24:13.020 --> 00:24:16.220
G-Goal!

00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:19.910
What an attack!

00:24:19.910 --> 00:24:22.830
Talk about lightning speed!

00:24:24.580 --> 00:24:27.870
Another goal for Yoin!

00:24:36.300 --> 00:24:37.510
<i>Why...</i>

00:24:45.960 --> 00:25:15.400
<b>Next Episode:
Tenacity To Win</b>

00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:50.760
Emperor Asuka's power 
is overwhelming.

00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:52.880
Repelled every time 
he takes him on,

00:24:52.880 --> 00:24:55.510
Kakeru has already accepted 
defeat in his heart.

00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:59.130
But just then, his late 
brother Suguru's voice

00:24:59.130 --> 00:25:00.640
echoes in his mind.

00:25:01.120 --> 00:25:03.570
Kakeru entrusts everything to it, 
even knowing there's no hope.

00:25:03.570 --> 00:25:06.750
What is Suguru trying to tell him?

00:25:06.750 --> 00:25:08.300
Next time on 
Knight in the Area,

00:25:08.300 --> 00:25:10.730
episode 24: "Tenacity to Win."

00:25:11.410 --> 00:25:15.060
Seven, my brother is with me now!
